@startsalt
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: the resolved layout of one screenful, and how a gated element is drawn in it
' covers: internal/choiceui/choiceui.go, internal/choiceui/gated_reason_test.go
' covers: internal/run/choices.go
' covers: internal/run/model_row.go
' Sibling of choice-prompt-render.puml, which owns the gating logic and the prose.
' This file owns only the resolved layout: what the operator confronts once
' applicableRows, comingSoon, gateAddons and gateEvidence have already executed.
'
' The checkboxes are grouped into two PLANES, each named by its own divider:
' execution (where the agent runs) and interface (what it can drive). One
' undifferentiated "add-ons" row put a Docker daemon beside a browser as though
' they answered the same question, and named only the first group because the
' divider was inferred from "the first multi-select row" rather than declared.
' Source: internal/choiceui/choiceui.go draw(); internal/run/choices.go row builders.
'
' Salt possesses no conditional construct. Optionality is consequently encoded,
' never branched — the five encodings are demonstrated below and named in the
' legend. The variant that eliminates the form entirely (no TTY) has no frame.
'
' The models row shows the BRIDGE OUTPUT, not the role vars the operator set.
' defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh maps ARCHITECT_MODEL (falling back to
' EDITOR_MODEL) into ANTHROPIC_MODEL, and SMALL_MODEL into
' ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL — two slots, so a third role var is never read.
' Bridge dialects for the other harnesses: _spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml.
'
' NOT drawn here, and all of it shipped: the topology strip under the hints, and
' the three regions the form is now painted in — a droppable head, a scrolling
' body indented two columns for its gutter, and a foot that follows the body.
'   the mechanism ..... _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-strip.puml
'   the regions ....... _spec/internal/choiceui/viewport.puml
'   every frame ....... _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-states.puml
'   still unbuilt ..... _spec/internal/choiceui/figure-fidelities.puml (the side pane)
' This file stays the resolved layout of one screenful, at a size that holds it.

' ── THE DEVICES ROW PACKS; TUI AND DESKTOP ARE ONE RADIO (2026-10-24) ──────
' User: "has empty spaces for browser/android/ios, avoid that. Show chrome and
' desktop directly there … Remove the disabled option in tui (radio button
' style) let the user choose tui or desktop". layoutInterface keeps the
' canonical order (tui, desktop, browser, android, ios, the rest) but packs the
' columns 0..n-1, so a harness without browser/android/ios shows no gaps
' (hermes: (•) tui  ( ) desktop  [ ] chrome). Where a harness offers desktop,
' tui stops being a locked [X]: Row.RadioSet draws tui and desktop as radios
' inside the checkbox row, pairTUIDesktop keeps exactly one on (the newer tick
' wins, an empty radio snaps back), and tui never enters the add-on list.
' Elsewhere tui stays the fixed [X] of addonFixed.
' Pinned by TestTheDevicesRowPacksItsOptionsWithoutGaps,
' TestTUIAndDesktopAreOneRadioChoice (internal/run) and
' TestARadioSetDrawsRadiosBesideCheckboxes (internal/choiceui).
'
' ── THE AUTH ROW IS AN AXIS, AND IT IS ORDERED BY RISK ─────────────────────
' Three options, always drawn in this order, because the prompt labels the row's
' horizontal as "◀ riskier ... safer ▶" and reading it left to right has to mean
' something:
'   usage credits ... metered per token against raw provider key material sitting
'                     in the environment for the agent to read. Unbounded spend,
'                     and the key is a file or a variable the agent can reach.
'   subscription .... a fixed-cost plan credential, and where it is a login on
'                     disk proveo suppresses env tokens over it. The failure this
'                     row exists to stop runs one way only — a subscription run
'                     silently billed per token, never the reverse.
'   local model ..... the safe end. Weights on this machine: nothing billed, and
'                     no credential for the agent or the egress hop to carry.
'                     COMING SOON — `--local-model` already runs the Ollama
'                     sidecar, but nothing routes THIS row to it, so it is drawn
'                     and gated rather than left out. The axis is where an
'                     operator looks to find out an option exists.
'
' AN UNAVAILABLE OPTION IS GATED, NEVER DROPPED. cursor's CLI has no
' bring-your-own-key path, so "usage credits" is off with the reason attached —
' dropping it is what made "cursor ignores my ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" something the
' operator could only discover by running. The reason goes in OffWhy, per option,
' so it appears under the option the cursor is on rather than as one row-wide
' string; Reason keeps the joined form for the row.
'
' comingSoon is NOT used here. It reallocates Off on every call, so gating two of
' three through it silently un-gates the first — the auth row gates its own
' options and picks a new Selected when the remembered one landed on a gate.
'
' AND A GATED OPTION ON A SINGLE-SELECT ROW EXPLAINS ITSELF THROUGH Reason, NOT
' OffWhy. cycle() skips an Off option on a single-select row — correctly, it
' cannot be chosen — so the cursor never lands on it and the per-option OffWhy
' is text nothing will ever display. helpLines suppressed the row-level Reason
' the moment the row carried any Help, which is exactly the shape of the auth
' row: cursor drew `usage credits` greyed out and said NOTHING about why, the
' one thing drawing it was supposed to communicate. The egress row escaped this
' only by carrying no Help map.
'
' A Multi row is not affected and keeps its old behaviour: cycle() moves onto
' gated options there and toggle() refuses, so its OffWhy is reachable and
' repeating Reason beside it would double the add-on rows up.
'
' THE HINT IS THE HALF THAT MAKES THE NOUNS MEAN SOMETHING. Under each option:
' what it is, then what it is made of on THIS host — host env variable names and
' the login file path when a login is what will be spent — then what choosing it
' withholds. It does not name a project .env: that file is not a credential
' surface. SPEC: _spec/internal/credentials/credential-decisions.puml
'
title Choice prompt wireframe — resolved layout, and how a gated element is drawn

{
{+
  {
    <&terminal> proveo SOLUTIONS | proveo/sandbox: portable, safe AI coding agents
  }
  ==run claudecode — confirm or change this run
  {
    git: | monorepo on <color:#00BAC6>rs-295-integration-discriminator</color> <i>(uncommitted changes)</i>
    keys: | ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
    tooling: | node  nx  python  docker
    subagents: | 7 definition(s)
    hooks: | .claude/settings.json
    llms: | <color:#00BAC6>main=claude-opus-5 (anthropic)</color>   <color:#00BAC6>small=claude-haiku-4-5 (anthropic)</color>
  }
  ~~
  {
    . | ◀ riskier | . | . | safer ▶
    ▸ egress | (X) allow-all | . | ( ) balanced | ( ) deny-all
    credentials | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>forward</color> | . | . | (X) broker
    model | ( ) Qwen 3.8 | (X) API keys | ( ) plan | ( ) Glimmer
    . | . | ———— execution ———— | . | .
    . | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>host</color> | (X) <color:#9a9a9a>sandbox</color> | . | .
    . | . | ———— interface ———— | . | .
    devices | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui</color> | [ ] browser | [ ] android | [ ] ios
    outputs | ( ) filtered | (X) verbose | . | .
  }
  --
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel
  ..
  always on: Mount the current git project in a sandbox for the agent
}
{
{^"1 · greyed — comingSoon"
  credentials | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>forward</color> | . | . | <color:#9a9a9a>(X) broker</color>
  .
  Rendered, never selectable: the whole
  credentials row is locked like egress.
  Arrows hover each mode to read it; the
  answer stays broker. A withheld option
  is not misread as nonexistent.
  (Until 2026-10-16 the example was the
  review tier, now deleted.)
}
{^"2 · empty cell — option withdrawn"
  credentials | . | . | . | (X) broker
  .
  The slot persists, so surviving options
  retain the column they occupied while
  the full complement was offered. broker
  stays in column 4, the safest.
}
{^"3 · absent region — applicableRows"
  . | ◀ riskier | . | . | safer ▶
  credentials | ( ) forward | . | . | (X) broker
  .
  An axis with nothing to determine is
  eliminated wholesale. The legend
  survives while one ordered row remains.
}
{^"4 · one answer — a radio, not a gated pair"
  outputs | ( ) filtered | (X) verbose
  execution | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>host</color> | (X) <color:#9a9a9a>sandbox</color>
  .
  Brackets say "any number of these" and
  parentheses "one of these". Evidence is
  genuinely one-of, so it is a radio row and
  the gate that kept two boxes exclusive —
  leaving "neither" reachable — is gone.
  .
  Execution is one-of by construction (a run
  has one place it runs) and now carries ONE
  box: the sidecar that made "neither" reachable
  is retired, so the row is greyed and ticked —
  a fact, not a question.
}
{^"5 · filtered — the bridge never reads it"
  set by operator | <color:#00BAC6>ARCHITECT_MODEL</color> | <color:#9a9a9a><s>EDITOR_MODEL</s></color> | <color:#00BAC6>SMALL_MODEL</color>
  claudecode reads | <color:#00BAC6>ANTHROPIC_MODEL</color> | . | <color:#00BAC6>ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL</color>
  prompt shows | <color:#00BAC6>main=</color> | . | <color:#00BAC6>small=</color>
  .
  Claude Code routes internally and exposes two slots, so ""EDITOR_MODEL"" is a
  fallback that never fires once ""ARCHITECT_MODEL"" is set. Printing all three
  role vars advertises an assignment the harness cannot honour, so the header
  shows the resolved slots instead — and every slot it shows is highlighted,
  because a half-highlighted row reads as one model mattering more than another.
}
{^"7 · described — the cursor's option explains itself, BELOW the hint"
  devices | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui</color> | [X] browser | [ ] android | [ ] ios
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel | . | . | .
  <color:#00BAC6>› ios — an iOS Simulator on this host — coming soon</color> | . | . | .
  <color:#9a9a9a>off: coming soon — not built yet</color> | . | . | .
  .
  The picker could only ever explain what it had taken AWAY: ""Reason"" is written
  when an option is gated off, so the add-ons that were available and ticked
  carried no text and "browser" had to be inferred from its name.
  ""Help"" describes the option the CURSOR is on, one row at a time — describing
  every option of every row at once is the wall of text this replaces.

  WRAPPED, never appended to the row: the row is already ~70 columns of
  checkboxes, so text placed after them runs off the terminal, which is how the
  one description the picker did have ended mid-sentence. The row's own
  ""Reason"" is still drawn inline and is now clipped with an ellipsis — it is a
  glance signal for a row the cursor is not on, and the same words are here in
  full.

  **Pinned LAST, under the hint, with nothing drawn after it.** Under its own row
  the block's height changed with the cursor and shoved every row beneath it up
  and down — the form moved while the operator was reading it. At the bottom it
  can grow freely and nothing above ever shifts.

  A greyed box that is TICKED reads "always on:" rather than "off:": it is not
  unavailable, it is compulsory, and the other label would say the opposite of
  what the checkbox shows.
}
{^"8 · fixed — a box that states a fact"
  execution | ( ) <color:#9a9a9a>host</color> | (X) <color:#9a9a9a>sandbox</color> | .
  devices | [X] <color:#9a9a9a>tui</color> | [ ] browser | [ ] android | [ ] ios
  .
  Greyed, and left in the state it states. ""host"" is the alternative an operator
  might otherwise assume unticking the daemon selects — it never is, because
  proveo containerises every run — and the TUI is the interface for the whole
  session whether or not a browser joins it. Neither is reported as a selected
  add-on, and neither appears in the row's inline ""Reason"": a note greyed on
  every run teaches the operator to skip the line that sometimes matters.

  **The sandbox is greyed for the opposite reason: it is COMPULSORY.** A harness
  that declares sbx runs there and nowhere else, so the box is ticked and locked
  and its help line reads "always on: Mount the current git project in a
  sandbox for the agent". Unticking used to reach the docker backend behind egress
  sidecars — a weaker boundary one keystroke away — and that escape then became
  ""PROVEO_SBX=0"". Since 2026-10-16 there is no escape: the docker backend is
  deleted, and since 2026-10-17 ""PROVEO_SBX"" is simply unread. Like the
  two facts above it stays out of the row's inline ""Reason"": a note greyed on
  every run only teaches the operator to skip the line that sometimes matters.

  It is the one greyed box that IS reported as a selected add-on. ""Selections""
  drops every greyed option, which is right for the two facts above and wrong
  here: a compulsory sandbox dropped from the read-back once sent the run to
  the very backend the lock existed to remove; that backend is now deleted.
}
{^"6 · nerd, fallback ascii — PROVEO_GLYPHS"
  The per-language devicons of the ""lsp:"" header row left with that row
  (2026-10-30, LSP removal). The tiers still decorate status marks.
  .
  Devicons live in a range a Powerline-patched font does not carry, and a terminal
  cannot be asked whether its font holds a codepoint — so nerd is the tier an
  operator declares with ""=nerd"", and the undeclared default falls back to
  Safe, never to a guess autodetection makes.
}
{^"9 · model — one row: where the model comes from (every harness)"
  model | ( ) Qwen 3.8 | (X) API keys | ( ) plan | ( ) Glimmer
  <color:#00BAC6>› Qwen 3.8 — 27B, MLX, same as --local-model qwen3.8:27b-mlx on darwin/arm64</color> | . | . | . | .
  .
  ONE row picks the model source (2026-09-27). It merges what used to be two:
  the auth row (""usage credits"" · ""subscription"", drawn for a harness with a
  plan) and the local-model row. ""usage credits"" is drawn as ""API keys"" and
  ""subscription"" as ""plan"", so every harness reads the same cells. A harness
  with no plan (hermes) draws ""Qwen 3.8 | API keys | . | Glimmer"" —
  the plan column stays empty.
  The row name occupies 16 columns, marker included. credentials is the
  longest name; 12 would put its last letter on the first option.
  Every option row pins to the same four columns. OS, outputs, ports and apps
  included: a missing value leaves its column blank. A cell is at most 10 runes.
  ""docker (sandbox)"" paints ""sandbox"".
  allow-all and forward and Qwen and host and filtered share column 1,
  API keys and sandbox and browser and verbose share column 2,
  balanced and plan share column 3, deny-all and broker and Glimmer share column 4.
  27B and 30B live in the hint. Glimmer's hint still says Muse Glimmer.
  GGUF and MLX are the hint, not the label:
  darwin/arm64 says MLX (""qwen3.8:27b-mlx"", ""muse-glimmer:30b-mlx""), every
  other host says GGUF (""qwen3.8:latest"", ""muse-glimmer:latest"").
  Picking one on a plan harness also
  answers auth = ""local model"", which withholds the plan credential.
  ""--local-model <tag>"" preselects the option whose Ollama repo owns the tag and,
  untouched, keeps that exact tag; an unlisted tag is drawn as its own option. A
  REMEMBERED tag of a listed model is re-resolved to this host's build.
  cursor draws no local options: cursor-agent cannot target a custom endpoint
  (its --endpoint picks a Cursor backend; open feature request
  forum.cursor.com/t/cursor-cli-custom-endpoint-and-api-key-support/129424).
  SPEC: _spec/defs/hermes/hermes-paradigm.puml
}
}
}

legend bottom
  <color:#9a9a9a>grey text</color> — offered, never selectable; the violated constraint is drawn on the row
  a "." cell — element absent, column position preserved for the survivors
  a titled group box — region rendered only while its title predicate holds
  <s>struck</s> — cleared by a cross-row gate, or never read by this harness
  no frame whatsoever — no TTY, so the form is never drawn and resolved values stand
  a glyph before a label — accented marker; devicon by default, ASCII via PROVEO_GLYPHS=ascii
  a "›" line under a row — what the option the cursor is on does, wrapped; "off:" adds why it cannot be picked
end legend
@endsaltnote as PortsRow
  **2026-10-05: execution's row is "OS"; "ports" joins it.**
  The divider still reads ""execution""; its row label is
  ""OS"" (host · sandbox). The interface divider stays; its
  row label is ""devices"" (tui · browser · android · ios).
  Under OS, sbx only, a
  multi-select ""ports"" row offers each discovered dev
  port, all unticked. Past four, column 4 is ""...More""
  and a dropdown lists the rest.
  _spec/internal/devports/dev-ports.puml
end note

